    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:solar_furnace",
      "title": "Solar Furnace",
      "text": "Heliostats turn with the Sun and feed a parabolic mirror wall, which brings their light to a point. Concentrated ten thousand times, sunlight melts what no fuel flame can.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Works only by day, under open sky and without rain. Set the concentration and the shutter: the target heats to T = (\u03b1CG/\u03b5\u03c3)^(1/4), and must sit between the melting point and where the material boils off - or the crucible fails."
    },
